g Communication Services peers, with revenue growing 23%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $254K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $68K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["EverQuote, Inc. is a small-cap communication services business with a $1.0B market cap on $693M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +20% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +2.4pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at -31% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $90M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 13 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, with adequate 0.96\u00d7 cash conversion.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin -69.9\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.0% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 13% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.4\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Very elevated short interest (27.8% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Communication Services peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.1531947652040022},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Communication Services ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"High market volatility with VIX at 36, signaling elevated fear","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Widening credit spreads suggest growing stress in corporate debt markets","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"AI-generated content commoditisation \u2014 as creation costs collapse toward zero, content libraries lose pricing power and differentiation narrows.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Growing faster than most Communication Services peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Among the least levered in Communication Services \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"MAJOR LEAGUE VOLLEYBALL ANNOUNCES LANDMARK MEDIA AGREEMENT FOR THE 2027 SEASON, BRINGING PROFESSIONAL VOLLEYBALL TO MORE FANS THAN EVER","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/major-league-volleyball-announces-landmark-media-agreement-for-the-2027-season-bringing-professional-volleyball-to-more-fans-than-ever-302942564.html","date":"2026-11-17","timestamp":1794936480.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.74,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"\"IT'S TOO BIG,\" SAID NO ONE EVER RIDING JUICED BIKES SCRAMBLER MINI","source":"prnewswire.com","link